Widening Type Casting:
-Widening type casting is also known as implicit type casting in which a smaller type is converted into a larger type,
-it is done by the compiler automatically.

Narrowing Type Casting:
Narrowing type casting is also known as explicit type casting or explicit type conversion which is done by the programmer manually.
In the narrowing type casting a larger type can be converted into a smaller type.
When a programmer changes the variable type while writing the code. We can use the cast operator to change the type of the variable.
For example, double to int or int to double.
